  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration obligated $21B in contracts in FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The agency executed 1,021,947 awards with an average award size of $20.6K, and obligations were down 11.7% year over year. Fiscal totals moved from $17.7B in FY21 to $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, $23.8B in FY25, and $21B in FY26. Computer Systems Design Services received $4.4B and Engineering Services received $3.6B in FY2026 to date. Automobile Manufacturing received $2.4B. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $1.3B, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services received $1.2B, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $1.1B. Facilities Support Services, Other Individual and Family Services, Custom Computer Programming Services, and Other Computer Related Services received $619M, $556M, $492M, and $451M respectively. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC led vendors with $1.8B, followed by SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION with $903M and HII MISSION TECHNOLOGIES CORP with $773M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has General Services Administration contract spending trended recently?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $21B in FY2026 to date, down 11.7% year over year. Fiscal-year totals were $17.7B in FY21, $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, $23.8B in FY25, and $21B in FY26. Award activity totaled 1,021,947 awards with an average award size of $20.6K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the largest contract categories and top vendors for GSA?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services received $4.4B and Engineering Services received $3.6B in FY2026 to date. Automobile Manufacturing received $2.4B, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $1.3B, and R&D and other professional services received $1.2B and $1.1B. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC received $1.8B, SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION received $903M, and HII MISSION TECHNOLOGIES CORP received $773M."
      }
    ]
