      "q": "How much does General Services Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "General Services Administration obligated $21B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency executed 1,021,947 awards with an average award size of $20.6K, and obligations were down 11.7% year over year. Fiscal-year totals were $17.7B in FY21, $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, and $23.8B in FY25."
